# Copy to .env (gitignored) and fill in.
#
# This file holds ONLY the database credentials, separately from
# .env.local.example / .env.local, because the Prisma CLI (`prisma db push`,
# `prisma migrate`, etc.) auto-loads a file literally named `.env` and never
# reads `.env.local` — putting DATABASE_URL in .env.local would make every
# `pnpm prisma ...` command fail with "Environment variable not found" even
# after the credential is set, which looks identical to the credential still
# being missing. Next.js and this repo's tests/setup-env.ts both also load
# `.env`, so one file serves the Prisma CLI, the app, and the tests — no
# duplication needed.

# Neon Postgres. DATABASE_URL is the POOLED connection string (host contains
# "-pooler"); DIRECT_DATABASE_URL is the direct one, which Prisma Migrate
# requires because migrations cannot run over a pooled connection.
DATABASE_URL=
DIRECT_DATABASE_URL=
